// # Library Split Deep Read — Function Inventory & Cross-Seam Audit
//
// Logline: Verify whether handoff_library_split.oot proposals for btree_disk_ops, protein_translation, dispatch_worker are executable; flag every cross-seam call edge and type conflict.
//
// Setup: 3 source files plus their sibling types files were read in full. Every claim cites file:line. Pure inventory — no edits made.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Per-file function table with sibling, cross-seam callers, dep kind.
//   2. Top-level types and their cross-seam refs.
//   3. Verdict per file: executable / needs adjustment / fundamentally wrong.
//   4. Corrected sibling layout where the handoff is wrong.
//   5. Cross-cutting findings and recommended next steps.

// ## 1. btree_disk_ops.oo (395 lines, 7 pub fns, 0 types here)

// Functions and proposed-sibling placement (handoff §3):
//
// | Function                    | Sig                                  | Lines  | Sibling     | Cross-seam callers       | Kind |
// |-----------------------------|--------------------------------------|--------|-------------|--------------------------|------|
// | btree_node_key_at           | (BTreeNode, Int) -> Int              | 15-29  | A lookup    | 51, 67, 80, 323          | val  |
// | btree_node_val_at           | (BTreeNode, Int) -> Int              | 31-45  | A lookup    | 69                       | val  |
// | btree_node_find_key_index   | (BTreeNode, Int) -> Int              | 47-58  | A lookup    | 78, 304                  | val  |
// | btree_node_lookup_value     | (BTreeNode, Int) -> Int              | 60-74  | A lookup    | (none external)          | val  |
// | btree_node_insert_key_value | (BTreeNode, Int, Int) -> BTreeNode   | 76-225 | B insert    | (none external)          | val  |
// | btree_node_split_leaf       | (BTreeNode, Int) -> BTreeSplit       | 227-300| C split     | (none external)          | val  |
// | btree_node_remove_key       | (BTreeNode, Int) -> BTreeNode        | 302-395| D remove    | (none external)          | val  |

// Top-level: none. BTreeNode (btree_disk_types.oo:24), BTreeSplit (btree_disk_types.oo:60) imported.
//
// Cross-seam edges (caller sibling -> callee sibling):
//   A.key_at       <- B.insert (80), D.remove (323)
//   A.find_key_ix  <- B.insert (78),  D.remove (304)
//   A.val_at       <- A.lookup (69)         — internal.
//   A.key_at       <- A.find_key_index (51), A.lookup (67) — internal.
//
// 3+ from single sibling check: key_at has 4 callers distributed A,A,B,D (1+1+1+1).
// find_key_index has 2 callers B and D. No sibling has 3+ callers into A.
//
// Verdict: NEEDS ADJUSTMENT.
//   Reason: handoff §7 says "No new imports beyond what the originals already use" (only
//   ./btree_disk_types.oo is imported at line 13). After the split, B and D must import A to
//   call key_at and find_key_index. The handoff's own §3 acceptance test does not list
//   sibling-to-sibling imports. Constraint and shape are mutually exclusive.
//
// Corrected layout (3 siblings + door; meets "no new imports" by combining mutators):
//   btree_disk_ops.oo (door) re-exports 3 siblings. ~16 lines.
//   btree_disk_ops_lookup.oo  A: key_at, val_at, find_key_index, lookup_value.  ~63 body + 12 hdr = 75.
//   btree_disk_ops_split.oo   C: btree_node_split_leaf.                          ~74 + 12 = 86.
//   btree_disk_ops_mutate.oo  B+D: insert (76-225) + remove (302-395) = 244 body + 12 hdr = 256. AT LIMIT.
// Rationale: insert and remove share caller profile (both depend on A accessors). Merging
// removes the only "mutator<-accessor" cycle without adding new imports. If 4 siblings is
// preferred, drop the "no new imports" rule and let B, D add `import "./btree_disk_ops_lookup.oo";`.

// ## 2. protein_translation.oo (380 lines, 22 pub fns, 3 types)

// Functions and proposed-sibling placement (handoff §4):
//
// | Function                      | Sig                                 | Lines  | Sibling  | Cross-seam callers         | Kind |
// |-------------------------------|-------------------------------------|--------|----------|----------------------------|------|
// | int_pow4                      | (Int) -> Int                        | 40-45  | A types  | 55                         | val  |
// | int_pow32                     | (Int) -> Int                        | 47-52  | A types  | 301                        | val  |
// | dna_base_at                   | (Int, Int) -> Int                   | 54-57  | A types  | 68, 69, 70                 | val  |
// | dna_pack4                     | (Int,Int,Int,Int) -> Int            | 59-61  | A types  | (none)                     | -    |
// | codon_pack                    | (Int, Int, Int) -> Int              | 63-65  | A types  | 71                         | val  |
// | codon_at                      | (Int, Int) -> Int                   | 67-72  | A types  | 295, 365                   | val  |
// | codon_standard_aa             | (Int) -> Int                        | 74-175 | B codons | 296                        | val  |
// | codon_is_start_standard       | (Int) -> Int                        | 177-182| B codons | 367                        | val  |
// | codon_is_stop_standard        | (Int) -> Int                        | 184-195| B codons | (none — UNUSED in file)    | -    |
// | protein_aa_weight_da          | (Int) -> Int                        | 197-262| C aa     | 297                        | val  |
// | protein_aa_charge             | (Int) -> Int                        | 264-278| C aa     | 298                        | val  |
// | translate_empty               | () -> TranslateAcc                  | 280-289| D scan   | 322                        | val  |
// | translate_scan                | (Int, Int, Int, TranslateAcc) -> T  | 291-309| D scan   | 308 self, 322              | val  |
// | protein_translate_frame       | (Int, Int, Int) -> TranslateAcc     | 311-323| D scan   | 326, 361                   | val  |
// | protein_translate_nucleotides | (Int, Int) -> TranslateAcc          | 325-327| D scan   | 341                        | val  |
// | protein_estimate_molecular_wt | (TranslateAcc) -> Int               | 329-334| D scan   | 342                        | val  |
// | protein_estimate_net_charge   | (TranslateAcc) -> Int               | 336-338| D scan   | (none)                     | -    |
// | protein_sequence_new          | (Int, Int, Int) -> ProteinSequence  | 340-350| E seq    | (none external)            | val  |
// | protein_sequence_mw           | (ProteinSequence) -> Int            | 352-354| E seq    | (none)                     | -    |
// | protein_sequence_charge       | (ProteinSequence) -> Int            | 356-358| E seq    | (none)                     | -    |
// | protein_orf_new               | (Int, Int, Int) -> OrfRecord        | 360-376| E seq    | (none external)            | val  |
// | orf_is_complete               | (OrfRecord) -> Int                  | 378-380| E seq    | (none)                     | -    |

// Top-level types (handoff places all in A):
//   ProteinSequence : 14-20.  OrfRecord : 22-29.  TranslateAcc : 31-38.
// Cross-seam refs: D and E construct these; all must be visible in A.
//
// Cross-seam edges (caller -> callee):
//   A.codon_at               <- D.translate_scan (295), E.protein_orf_new (365)
//   A.int_pow32              <- D.translate_scan (301)
//   B.codon_standard_aa      <- D.translate_scan (296)
//   B.codon_is_start_stan.   <- E.protein_orf_new (367)
//   C.protein_aa_weight_da   <- D.translate_scan (297)
//   C.protein_aa_charge      <- D.translate_scan (298)
//   D.protein_translate_nucl.<- E.protein_sequence_new (341)
//   D.protein_estimate_mw    <- E.protein_sequence_new (342)
//   D.protein_translate_fr.  <- E.protein_orf_new (361)
//   B.codon_is_stop_standard <- (NONE — 184-195 is dead code in this file)
//
// 3+ from single sibling: D.translate_scan calls 4 distinct cross-sibling fns (A.codon_at,
// A.int_pow32, B.codon_standard_aa, C.protein_aa_weight_da, C.protein_aa_charge). E depends on
// 3 siblings (A, B, D). D depends on 3 siblings (A, B, C). Heavy cross-seam traffic.
//
// Verdict: NEEDS ADJUSTMENT.
//   Reason 1: same constraint contradiction as btree. Handoff §4 says 0 new imports, but D and E
//             must import 3 siblings each.
//   Reason 2: codon_pack (codon_table.oo:25), codon_standard_aa (codon_table.oo:29),
//             codon_is_start_standard (codon_table.oo:132), codon_is_stop_standard
//             (codon_table.oo:139) are byte-identical in codon_table.oo and protein_translation.oo.
//             Handoff §4 says "Do NOT shadow it" but creates protein_translation_codons.oo with
//             the same 100-line switch. NAME is preserved; CONTENT is duplicated.
//   Reason 3: protein_orf_new (E) calls codon_at (A) and codon_is_start_standard (B), straddling
//             two proposed seams.
//
// Corrected 2-sibling layout (RECOMMENDED; meets 256 cap, no sibling-to-sibling imports):
//   protein_translation.oo (door) imports codon_table.oo + 2 new siblings; re-exports all.
//   protein_translation_core.oo  A+B+C (lines 14-278).  ~265 body + 12 hdr = 277. Over by 21.
//                                  Fix: drop codon_is_stop_standard (dead code, see table).
//                                  277 - 11 = 266. Still 10 over. The 100-line
//                                  codon_standard_aa switch is the bulk. Best move: door imports
//                                  codon_table.oo and re-exports the 4 codon fns; core sibling
//                                  holds only types + AA + pack helpers (lines 14-72 + 197-278).
//                                  Body: 59 + 82 = 141 + 12 hdr = 153. OK.
//   protein_translation_api.oo   D+E (lines 280-380).   ~101 body + 12 hdr = 113. OK.
//                                  This sibling must import protein_translation_core.oo for
//                                  types and AA helpers. ONE new sibling import — drop the
//                                  "no new imports" rule for this one edge.
//                                  Alternative: drop AA helpers (C) into api sibling too; then
//                                  core sibling is types+pack only (lines 14-72, 73 lines) and
//                                  api sibling is D+E+C (190 lines). But this widens the seam.
// Rationale: codon_table.oo is the canonical decode table (bioinformatics.oo:17 imports it; the
// handoff's own "Do NOT shadow it" statement). Door re-imports codon_table.oo and re-exports
// the 4 codon fns. protein_translation.oo's local copy is removed in the move. The "Do NOT
// shadow" promise is honored by CONTENT (no duplicate), not just NAME.

