// Top-level types:
//   DispatcherConfig : dispatch_worker.oo:6-12   (5 fields)
//   SwarmDispatcher  : dispatch_worker.oo:14-23
//   WorkerNode       : dispatch_worker.oo:25-34
//   SwarmTask        : dispatch_worker.oo:36-47
//
// Cross-seam edges within dispatch_worker.oo: B.assign -> B.can_accept (141) — same sibling, internal.
// External consumers (not new imports): dispatch.oo:19,23,55,61,67 call dispatcher_config_init
// (5 args); dispatch.oo:28 calls worker_node_init; dispatch.oo:32,41,46 call swarm_task_create;
// dispatch.oo:37 calls worker_node_can_accept; dispatch.oo:42 calls task_is_terminal;
// dispatch.oo:47 calls task_can_retry; dispatch.oo:51,57,63,69 call engine fns.

// ## 4. THE CONFLICT: DispatcherConfig is NOT a duplicate
//
// dispatch_types.oo:6-9  : { strategy: Int, max_queue_depth: Int }              (2 fields)
// dispatch_worker.oo:6-12: { strategy, max_queue_depth, max_worker_capacity,
//                            default_timeout_ms, max_retries }                  (5 fields)
//
// Handoff §5 (lines 144-146) reads these as "duplicates" and proposes "Canonical def lives in
// dispatch_types.oo; dispatch_worker_types.oo imports it instead of redeclaring." This is
// EXECUTABLE-IMPOSSIBLE without scope expansion:
//
//   (a) 2-field vs 5-field are STRUCTURALLY DIFFERENT. oodac treats them as unrelated types.
//   (b) If dispatch_types.oo:6-9 is canonical, dispatcher_config_init at dispatch_worker.oo:73-79
//       (5-field literal) fails to compile — sets fields the type does not have.
//   (c) dispatch.oo:19, 23, 55, 61, 67 call dispatcher_config_init(0,32,4,1000,2) with 5 args.
//       The 5-arg form is load-bearing for the door.
//   (d) If dispatch_types.oo:6-9 stays untouched AND dispatch_worker_types.oo holds the 5-field
//       version, dispatch.oo imports BOTH (lines 13-14). oodac reports redefinition.
//
// Verdict: FUNDAMENTALLY WRONG. The "duplication" framing misreads the source.
// Resolution options (library lane must pick one; Options 1 and 2 need out-of-scope edits):
//   Option 1 (RECOMMENDED): Expand dispatch_types.oo:6-9 to the 5-field version. Remove the
//                           DispatcherConfig declaration from dispatch_worker.oo. All public
//                           symbols preserved. dispatch.oo:13 already pulls the canonical.
//   Option 2: Move DispatcherConfig out of dispatch_types.oo entirely. Delete lines 6-9 and
//             11-19. Declare only in dispatch_worker_types.oo. dispatcher_config_new and
//             dispatcher_config_depth (dispatch_types.oo:11, 18) must move with the type.
//   Option 3: Refactor door to use a unified 2-field DispatcherConfig. Changes API; contradicts
//             handoff §7 "this is a pure file move, not an API change".
// If library lane refuses scope expansion, the dispatch split is BLOCKED.

// ## 5. Cross-cutting findings

// 5.1 Constraint contradiction. Handoff §7 says "No new imports beyond what the originals
//     already use." Originals: btree_disk_ops.oo imports btree_disk_types.oo (line 13);
//     protein_translation.oo and dispatch_worker.oo import nothing. After the handoff's split,
//     protein_translation's D and E require 3 sibling imports each; btree's B and D require A.
//     The constraint is unsatisfiable. Either the rule is dropped, or siblings are re-bucketed
//     so each is closed under its caller set (see §1 and §2 corrected layouts). The rule also
//     forbids siblings importing each other, but the door MUST import each new sibling.
//     Re-word to "no new imports of UNRELATED std modules".

// 5.2 Symbol count drift. Handoff §4 says protein_translation has "23 public symbols". This
//     file has 22 pub fns + 3 types = 25. Handoff §5 says dispatch_worker has "17 public
//     symbols". This file has 15 pub fns + 4 types = 19. Counts low by 2-3. Re-state the
//     acceptance test as "all N pub fns and all M type names stay importable from the door".

// 5.3 codon_table.oo shadow. Handoff §4: "Do NOT shadow it" — preserved by NAME but violated
//     by CONTENT. The 4 codon fns are byte-identical in codon_table.oo and
//     protein_translation.oo. Recommended fix: door re-imports codon_table.oo; see §2.

// 5.4 Dead code. protein_translation.oo:184-195 (codon_is_stop_standard) is unused in this
//     file. protein_orf_new (line 366) tests acc.last_aa == 0 instead. Safe to drop; saves 11 lines.

// 5.5 Pre-existing (not caused by split). bioinformatics.oo:58 calls codon_standard_translate
//     (String) -> String. That symbol does not exist anywhere in ooda/std/. Grep returned only
//     the call site. Library lane owns this; audit lane notes.

// 5.6 library_status.oot impact. Status stays BLOCKED for all 3 files (oodac-bound, not
//     file-size bound per library_status.oot:13-19). No disagreement with handoff §1, §6.

// ## 6. Verdict summary
//
// | File                       | Proposed    | Verdict                | Blockers                                |
// |----------------------------|-------------|------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
// | btree_disk_ops.oo (395)    | 4 + door    | NEEDS ADJUSTMENT       | A<-B, A<-D require imports; merge       |
// |                            |             |                        | mutators (B+D) to keep 0 new imports.   |
// | protein_translation (380)  | 5 + door    | NEEDS ADJUSTMENT       | (a) D<-A,B,C and E<-A,B,D need imports |
// |                            |             |                        | (b) codon_table duplication             |
// |                            |             |                        | (c) protein_translation_core over 256   |
// | dispatch_worker.oo (323)   | 3 + door    | FUNDAMENTALLY WRONG    | DispatcherConfig is 2-field vs 5-field  |
// |                            |             |                        | distinct types, not duplicates.         |
// |                            |             |                        | dispatch_types.oo edit required         |
// |                            |             |                        | (out of scope per handoff §7).          |
//
// btree and protein splits are salvageable with re-bucketing. dispatch split is BLOCKED on a
// type-conflict resolution that requires editing a file the handoff marks out of scope.

// ## 7. Recommended next steps
//
// 1. Audit lane: route this report to the library lane. Ask whether Option 1 (edit
//    dispatch_types.oo to 5-field) or Option 2 (delete DispatcherConfig + its 2 helpers from
//    dispatch_types.oo) is acceptable. Block the dispatch split until answered.
// 2. Library lane: re-bucket btree and protein per §1 and §2 corrected layouts. Drop "no
//    new imports" only where unavoidable and document why. Drop codon_table.oo duplication
//    per §2; door re-imports codon_table.oo.
